---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';

const tree = `Salesdam-v3/
├── backend/              Express + Mongoose API
│   ├── app.js            Middleware and every route mount
│   ├── server.js         Bootstrap only
│   ├── config/
│   │   ├── db.js
│   │   └── objects/      Seed definitions for standard objects
│   ├── controllers/      Request handling, one per resource
│   ├── services/         Domain logic (formulaParser, rollupService, …)
│   ├── models/           Mongoose schemas
│   ├── middleware/       auth, tenant, permissions, rateLimiter
│   ├── routes/           Routers, mounted under /api/v1
│   ├── utils/            errors, validators, logger
│   └── scripts/          Seeds and one-off migrations
│
├── frontend/             React + Vite app
│   └── src/
│       ├── layout/       Sidebar, Topbar, Layout shell
│       ├── pages/        One folder per route
│       ├── components/   Reusable UI, common/ and feature folders
│       ├── context/      Auth, Tenant, App providers
│       ├── services/api/ Typed API wrappers
│       ├── hooks/
│       ├── utils/
│       └── styles/       variables.css (design tokens) + global.css
│
├── docs/                 This site (Astro, static)
│   └── src/
│       ├── data/         navigation.js, openapi.js, searchIndex.js
│       ├── components/   Header, Sidebar, SearchModal, ApiExplorer, AccessGate
│       ├── layouts/      MainLayout.astro
│       ├── pages/        One .astro file per documentation page
│       ├── utils/        schema.js — OpenAPI helpers
│       └── styles/       tokens.css + global.css
│
└── landing/              Marketing site (Astro)`;

const LAYERS = [
  ['routes/', 'Declare paths and attach middleware. No logic.'],
  ['controllers/', 'Read the request, call services, shape the response. Own the HTTP concerns.'],
  ['services/', 'Domain logic, independent of HTTP. Unit-testable in isolation.'],
  ['models/', 'Mongoose schemas and their hooks.'],
  ['middleware/', 'Cross-cutting concerns: authentication, tenancy, permissions, rate limiting.'],
];
---

<MainLayout
  title="Project Structure"
  description="How the repository is laid out and which layer owns what."
>
  <h1>Project Structure</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    One repository, four deployable applications. They share no code — the
    boundary between them is the HTTP API.
  </p>

  <pre><code>{tree}</code></pre>

  <h2>Backend layers</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Directory</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {LAYERS.map(([dir, role]) => (
          <tr><td><code>{dir}</code></td><td>{role}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Every route mount lives in <code>backend/app.js</code>.</strong>
    <code>server.js</code> is a 14-line bootstrap. If you're looking for the base
    path a router is served under, <code>app.js</code> is the only place to check.
  </div>

  <h2>Where the interesting logic lives</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Concern</th><th>File</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Formula parsing and evaluation</td><td><code>services/formulaParser.js</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Formula values on records</td><td><code>services/formulaService.js</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rollup aggregation</td><td><code>services/rollupService.js</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Field validation</td><td><code>services/validationService.js</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Structured validation engine</td><td><code>services/validationEngine.js</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>List-view filters and operators</td><td><code>services/listViewService.js</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Auth and API keys</td><td><code>middleware/auth.js</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Object and field metadata</td><td><code>models/ObjectMeta.js</code>, <code>models/FieldMeta.js</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Record storage</td><td><code>models/DynamicRecord.js</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Frontend conventions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      One folder per component or page, containing <code>X.jsx</code> and
      <code>X.module.css</code>, imported as
      <code>import styles from './X.module.css'</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      All colours, spacing and radii come from tokens in
      <code>src/styles/variables.css</code>. Using a raw hex loses dark mode, which
      is defined as a token override on <code>[data-theme='dark']</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      API calls go through <code>src/services/api/</code> rather than calling
      <code>fetch</code> from a component.
    </li>
    <li>Server state is React Query; UI state is context or local state.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The metadata model</h2>
  <p>
    Records are not stored in per-object collections. <code>ObjectMeta</code> and
    <code>FieldMeta</code> describe what an object <em>is</em>, and every record of
    every object lives in <code>DynamicRecord</code> with its values in a
    <code>data</code> map. That is why one set of endpoints serves custom and
    standard objects alike, and why adding a field requires no migration.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>The storage shape is not the wire shape.</strong> Values live under
    <code>data</code> in MongoDB but are flattened to top-level keys in API
    responses. Don't send <code>{'{ data: { … } }'}</code> to the record endpoints.
  </div>
</MainLayout>
